Architecture plan for issues #87-#92

Project shape
- Next.js App Router application with public blog pages under app/(public), admin editor under app/admin, shared storage/database utilities under lib, and UI styling through Tailwind/editorial theme tokens.
- Existing uploaded post images are stored through lib/storage/object-storage.ts and referenced by relative object keys in database-backed post records.

Issue grouping and dependencies
- #87, #88: Homepage-only presentation changes in app/(public)/page.tsx. These can be applied independently, but should be reviewed together to preserve the Official Journal layout hierarchy.
- #89, #90: Article page typography changes in app/(public)/blog/[slug]/page.tsx. These are independent CSS class changes but should share heading scale decisions with homepage typography.
- #92: Shared 16:9 cover treatment spans homepage cards and article cover. Prefer a small shared class/string helper for cover media classes to avoid divergent aspect-ratio rules.
- #91: Admin post editor enhancement. Add a client-only cover image cropper component colocated under app/admin/posts/_components. It must preserve the existing multipart form/server action flow by assigning the cropped File/Blob to the existing coverImage field before submit, rather than introducing a separate upload endpoint.

Key design decisions
- Keep content/markup stable for visual-only issues; only remove requested intro copy and adjust Tailwind classes.
- Define/reuse 16:9 media styling once where practical, using aspect-[16/9] overflow-hidden and object-cover for consistency across homepage and article pages.
- For the cropper, avoid new persistence paths. Use browser File APIs/canvas in a client component, keep file size/type validation consistent with existing server-side upload constraints, and maintain accessible controls for crop preview and confirmation.
- No new auth or email platform integrations are required by these issues.

Validation plan
- Run npm test and npm run lint after each issue when relevant.
- For cropper work, also verify admin editor form still submits multipart/form-data and that server actions receive coverImage under the existing field name.
